Name: TouchPad: light sensor off
Version: 3.1.0-1
Author: NotAlexNoyle
Description: Stop sensord polling a dead ambient light sensor (ISL29023 at I2C 0x44): the sensor is taken out of the sensor framework driver list in /etc/usd. The kernel's 45-100 log lines a second about it stop, sensord drops from a fifth to a sixth of a core, system time from 16 to 11 percent. Restart sensord (or reboot) after applying; automatic brightness is lost (it already was). Made from webOS CE 3.1.0 files; the two files are the stock 3.0.5 ones too.

--- .orig/etc/usd/usd_topaz-Wifi_default.xml
+++ /etc/usd/usd_topaz-Wifi_default.xml
@@ -109,7 +109,11 @@
 			<pluginFilename>./lib/cypress_abd_ver1.0.so</pluginFilename>
 			<pluginInitFunction>cypress_abc_alloc</pluginInitFunction>
 		</cypress_abc> -->
-		<isl29023>
+		<!-- The ambient light sensor (ISL29023 at I2C 0x44) is taken out of the driver list by the patch
+		     net.riverstonerelay.patches.touchpad-light-sensor-off: on a tablet whose sensor no longer answers,
+		     sensord polled it ten times a second and failed every time (45-100 kernel log lines a second, a fifth
+		     of a core for sensord, the system log rotating every few minutes). Removing the patch restores this.
+		<isl29023-off>
 			<debugLevel>1</debugLevel>
 			<pluginFilename>libusd_drv_isl29023_als.so</pluginFilename>
 			<pluginInitFunction>_isl29023_alloc</pluginInitFunction>
@@ -126,7 +130,8 @@
 				<als_adc_resolution>1</als_adc_resolution>
 				<als_rangek>0</als_rangek>
 			</ils_proximity_als>
-		</isl29023>
+		</isl29023-off>
+		-->
 	</config>
 </drivers>
 
